WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:05.031
[Music]

00:00:05.031 --> 00:00:08.800
[Sandra Occhipinti]
The NLM Herb Garden is uh is one of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:13.840
demonstration gardens that are maintained&nbsp;
by Montgomery County Master Gardeners.

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:23.209
We're here two to three hours, one day a week, to&nbsp;
maintain the garden, plant, mulch, weed, trim.

00:00:23.209 --> 00:00:28.820
[Pat Kenny]
This was a&nbsp;part of the National Institutes of Health&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:34.360
celebration of the Bicentennial in 1976.

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:41.080
The Potomac Unit Herb Society of America was&nbsp;
asked to take over the care of the garden.

00:00:41.080 --> 00:00:45.600
It was a blessing for me because I lived close by.

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:47.960
I was interested in herbal plants.

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:49.956
I was interested in good health.

00:00:50.031 --> 00:00:55.520
[Occhipinti]
So Rosemary, we think of as a culinary herb.

00:00:55.520 --> 00:01:00.000
Rosemary is said to improve&nbsp;
memory and concentration.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:05.920
It was also used to cure headaches. And there&nbsp;
are a lot of culinary herbs in this garden.

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:07.760
And they were all used medicinally.

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:09.566
This is Valerian.

00:01:09.566 --> 00:01:14.949
It was used for insomnia and as a sedative.

00:01:14.949 --> 00:01:16.719
[Kenny]
But most of the culinary&nbsp;herbs,&nbsp;

00:01:16.719 --> 00:01:22.880
most of the herbs we use for&nbsp;
cooking, have antibacterial, antiviral,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:32.848
anti-inflammatory, and all kinds of phytochemicals&nbsp;
constituents that nowadays we know are medicinal.

00:01:33.647 --> 00:01:43.601
What I love about this garden is this&nbsp;
shows some of the history of medicine.

00:01:44.326 --> 00:01:46.549
[Occhipinti]
One of the times that&nbsp;I was in the garden, &nbsp;

00:01:46.549 --> 00:01:54.040
and a young man, a patient&nbsp;
from the Clinical Center, came into the garden.

00:01:54.040 --> 00:01:59.000
And he said "Excuse me, I walk here. I walk to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:06.244
this garden every day and I just&nbsp;
wanted to thank you... for it."

00:02:07.738 --> 00:02:12.360
And it was, I was a complete mess.&nbsp;
But it was still, you know, with a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:19.572
garden and you've got textures and colors&nbsp;
and flowers and and it's always changing.

00:02:19.572 --> 00:02:27.400
And it it was very important&nbsp;
therapeutically to him.

00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:29.760
And it's certainly therapeutic to work in it.

00:02:29.844 --> 00:02:34.680
[Music]

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:39.000
[Music fades to silence]

